# Clinical AI Guardrails (Physio-Shield)

Applies to `src/ai/**` and the Gemini proxy Edge Function. PHI Safety (AGENTS.md Iron Rule 1) is absolute.

## PHI Isolation

- Never send full patient names, MRNs, phones, emails, or raw identifiable notes to Gemini.
- Use initials / `[Patient]` placeholders; prefer the proxy’s de-identification path (`deidentifyText` / scrubbed generation).
- Client AI modules must call the approved proxy (`gemini-proxy`), not Google APIs with keys in the browser.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
console.log('Insight for', patient.fullName, payload);
await fetch(GEMINI_URL_WITH_KEY, { body: JSON.stringify({ text: clinicalNote }) });

// ✅ GOOD
// Log only non-identifying codes; send de-identified context via gemini-proxy
await invokeGeminiProxy({ generation, patientInitials: 'A.B.' });
```

## Prompt & Output Safety

- Keep clinical system prefixes that forbid echoing full names.
- Do not persist model outputs that reintroduce identifiers into logs or unencrypted stores.
- Cap payloads; respect therapist vs patient body-size limits on the proxy.
- Treat model output as advisory—never auto-write diagnoses, plans, or status changes without therapist/service-layer confirmation.

## Sync With Clinical State

- AI suggestions that affect plans, freezes, or statuses must go through `src/services/` and keep JSONB/local state in sync (Iron Rule 4).
- Do not invent schema fields for “AI metadata”; use existing columns/migrations only (Iron Rule 3).
